Subject: Merge the field operand loads

What this does
  Merge the field operand loads.

Why we need it
  A named-field read decoded `d` and `r` with two separate 2-byte loads; they are adjacent in the instruction.

What it adds
  One 4-byte load plus two shifts for `d`/`r` in `get_field`/`get_field2`. The same trick for the store's `site`/`v` pair was and reverted.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
